hen we compared the analytes in  human Neuroscience panel 2 with the  established biomarkers in the human  amyloid beta and tau kit we saw that  both neuro Grandon and fa beeeep III  correlated with phospho tau while the  significance of these associations is  unclear the take-home message is that  multiplexing can expose patterns that  may not otherwise be discovered  I would like to transition to talking  about the newest addition to our amino  acid portfolio the SMC X Pro and its  associated kits for single molecule  counting  SMC stands for single molecule counting  and the general assay principle is shown  in the schematic below the SMC  immunoassay it follows the same  rationale as a traditional sandwich  Eliza with an SMC kit you have capture  and detection reagents that form a  sandwich complex the capture antibody is  coated on two magnetic beads while the  detection antibody is labeled with a  fluorophore what distinguishes the SMC  assay is a proprietary Aleutian step  where the sandwich complex dissociates  and the individual fluorescently  labelled detection antibodies are  digitally counted to get an idea of the  typical SMC workflow I've reiterated the  assay steps below and included volumes  and plate types so most of the assay  setup occurs in a 96-well plate the  initial incubation is 200 microlitre  volume 100 microliters of that is the  sample or standard and the other 100  microliters is the capture bead the  plates is then transferred to a magnet  and washed before the addition of 20  microliters of detection antibody and  then incubation to generate the sandwich  complex the plate then goes through a  series of washes to remove excess  detection antibody prior to the aleutian  step after the aleutian the capture  beads can be magnetically separated  allowing the researcher to isolates the  lu8  which contains the label detection  antibody this toilet is transferred to a  384-well plate containing the  neutralization buffer after the  neutralization step the SI is ready to  be analyzed on an SMC  instruments  currently our Millah poor Sigma SMC kits  can be run on two instruments the arena  which is the first generation fluidics  driven system and the new SMC X Pro  which is the second generation platform  the data table highlights the  specifications of each system both  instruments read from a 384 well plate  some of the improvements to the SMC x  pro include a smaller footprint so it's  a true benchtop instrument and a more  rapid runtime which allows researchers  to run an experiments generate and  analyze data all on the same day as well  as a simplified readout the arena had  took the Reina took three measurements  which were tected events event photons  and total photons and that produced  three standard curves and utilizes  weighted algorithm to incorporate the  three measurements and assign sample  values the SMC X Pro just uses a single  readout which is response and that is  generated by a scanning confocal laser  which surveys the sample wells of a 384  well plate digitally counting molecules  of fluorescently labelled detection  antibody  we have recently released an SMC kit for  the amyloid-beta  42 peptide this kit has been validated  in accordance with the benchmarks  described earlier for the measurement of  amyloid beta 42 in cerebrospinal fluid  and a 1 to 20 dilution and in plasma at  a 1 to 4 dilution from the standard  curve on the Left  generated on the SMC X Pro you can see  that the assay sensitivity is not an  issue for this kit as the wounded Swain  diluted normal CSF samples overlaid onto  the standard curve are falling in the  middle of the curve to give you an idea  of the consistency between the SMC  instruments on the right you can see the  excellent correlation of these CSF  samples when their values were compared  between when they were obtained on the  arena and then on the second generation  SMC X Pro and there's again excellent  correlation the bottom figure  demonstra